# What these are, at source

`wrap_verifier.ml:539-616` builds `x_hat` as an MSM whose base for public-input entry `i` is
`lagrange ~domain srs i` (`:207-224`) or the base half of
`lagrange_with_correction ~input_length:n ~domain srs i` (`:247-291`). Both read

    (Kimchi_bindings.Protocol.SRS.Fp.lagrange_commitment srs d i).unshifted = [| Finite g |]

at `d = 2 ^ Domain.log2_size domains.h`. `wrap_main`'s `~srs` is the **STEP** URS
(`Backend.Tick.Keypair.load_urs ()`), and `Backend.Tick = Kimchi_backend.Pasta.Vesta_based_plonk`
— so these are **VESTA** points and their coordinates live in **Fq**, the wrap circuit's own field.
`Common.Max_degree.step_log2 = Backend.Tick.Rounds.n = 16` (`common.ml:6-9`), so `d = 65536`.

