`SRS::<G>::create(depth)` is DETERMINISTIC: `g[i] = point_of_random_bytes(map, Blake2b512(i as u32
big-endian))` (`poly-commitment/src/ipa.rs:532-542`), which is the same code path
`Kimchi_bindings.Protocol.SRS.Fp.create` runs inside Mina. `PALLAS_G_HEAD_XY` below is
`SRS::<Pallas>::create(16).g` out of the SAME binary, and
`Dregg2.Circuit.Emit.MinaStepSrsLagrangePin.srs_construction_is_the_devnet_srs` proves it equals
the first sixteen generators of the **devnet blockchain Wrap SRS** — a list this module does not
own, dumped from a real Mina node by `wrap_group_export.rs`. Two independent sources, not a
constant against its own definition.

# The correction, and upstream's own TODO

`lagrange_with_correction` returns `(g, negate (pow2pow g actual_shift))` with
`actual_shift = Ops.bits_per_chunk * Ops.chunks_needed ~num_bits:input_length` — `input_length`,
NOT `input_length - 1`, which upstream flags with its own TODO (`wrap_verifier.ml:249-252`) while
`scale_fast2` uses `chunks_needed ~num_bits:(num_bits - 1)` (`plonk_curve_ops.ml:252-256`). At 255
and at 128 the two expressions agree (51 and 26 chunks), so the correction cancels `scale_fast2`'s
`+ 2 ^ actual_bits_used` exactly. `CORRECTION_XY` is computed at upstream's LITERAL expression, not
at the one the TODO says it should be.

`CORRECTION_XY` is indexed over the **non-one-bit** entries only, in order: a one-bit entry takes
the `Cond_add` path and `wrap_verifier.ml:588-594` filters it out of the correction reduce
entirely. `WIDTHS` is the per-entry packed width, and its census is 15 x 255, 40 x 128, 12 x 1. -/
